  "observed": [
    "Each of eight installed consumers read a value captured by the application initializer, made a synchronous file read, awaited a scheduled file read, pulled one item, and closed the iterator. The independent harness verified the previous contents were replaced with 'closed'.",
    "Ordinary and reviewed artifacts agreed on the per-entry and phase-specific capabilities. Receipt verification authenticated all archive references before installation.",
    "Real Lean interfaces distinguished clock, randomness, process information and stdio from a plain IO signature. No runtime sandbox, registry publication or other language profile is claimed.",
    "Unpermitted startup, worker, iterator-only close, process-wide directory mutation, and eagerly computed debug output each stopped a real build without a handoff. A startup write sentinel was not executed by inspection.",
    "Existing Retained and Pulse fixtures needed no ambient grants. Depot's leased-resource and close paths required filesystem. A generated Python host member remained a separate host capability."
  ],
  "reproduce": {
    "build": "LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_EFFECT_TEST=1 LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_EFFECT_EVIDENCE=/absolute/path/to/new-releases node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/helpers/native-effect-policy.mjs",
    "replay": "LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_EFFECT_REPLAY=/absolute/path/to/original-releases node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/helpers/native-effect-policy.mjs",
    "prerequisites": "Use pinned Lean, native C/C++, CPython, and Rust tooling for the build; configure CARGO_HOME with the locked task-runtime dependencies for offline Cargo. Replay uses the original handoffs and host installation tools without compiling Lean."
  },
